{
  "_comment": [
    "DRAWABLE SKELETONS for every row in components.md — the structured half of that file (#609).",
    "",
    "WHY A SIDECAR AND NOT PROSE. `components.md` describes anatomy, keyboard contract, ARIA and",
    "Turbo behaviour, because that is what BUILDING a component requires. A recipe is in there too",
    "(`bg-muted`, `text-step--1`), but embedded in sentences — and regex-parsing generated prose is",
    "the failure `derived-artifacts` exists to prevent. So the drawable skeleton lives here, in a",
    "form a generator can read without guessing, and the prose stays the thing a builder reads.",
    "",
    "WHAT AN ENTRY IS FOR. `pen_library.py` mirrors the design system into pen so an agent can",
    "compose against the SAME components it will build the real code from. An entry is therefore a",
    "skeleton — enough to recognise and place the component — never a reimplementation of it. If an",
    "entry starts carrying interaction or a11y detail, it has stopped being a projection.",
    "",
    "EVERY ROW APPEARS, and `scripts/check_component_shapes.py` fails if one does not. A row that",
    "cannot be drawn says so with `drawable: false` and a reason: silence would let the pen library",
    "look complete while a composition picks a component that is not there.",
    "",
    "FILLS ARE ROLE TOKENS, never hex. A shape referencing a role the pack does not declare is",
    "reported and left out rather than given an invented colour.",
    "",
    "parts[]:  kind = box | pill | text | field | line | avatar | icon-slot | column",
    "          fill/stroke/color = a role token name, without the leading `--`",
    "          span = how many grid columns the part occupies within its row (default 1)"
  ],

